# Project Context

Project: Purchase Patterns
Subtitle: An End-to-End Retail Machine Learning System

Dataset: UCI Online Retail II, obtained from Kaggle.
Domain: Customer Analytics.

Business goals:
1. Analyze customer purchase behavior.
2. Perform customer segmentation.
3. Predict repeat purchases within the next 60 days.
4. Support evidence-based retention targeting.

# Technology

- Python 3.12
- uv for dependency management
- SQL, DuckDB, Parquet, dbt
- scikit-learn, XGBoost, LightGBM
- Optuna for hyperparameter optimization
- MLflow for experiment tracking
- Pytest and Ruff for code quality

Add dependencies only when needed.

# Engineering Standards

- Write clean, modular, readable Python.
- Prefer reusable functions over notebook-only code.
- Add type hints and docstrings.
- Write tests for new functionality.
- Keep changes small and focused.
- Explain architectural decisions.
- Do not introduce unnecessary frameworks.

# Data Science Standards

- Prevent data leakage.
- Features must use only data available before prediction time.
- The 60-day repeat-purchase target must use future transactions.
- Keep training, validation, and test data separate.
- Never tune hyperparameters on the final test set.
- Do not invent model performance or business results.

# Safety and Workflow

- Never commit raw datasets or credentials.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Do not automatically commit or push code.
- Present an implementation plan before large changes.
- Run relevant tests after implementing a feature.
- Summarize what changed and why.